cast:
  Kit:
  Grace:
  Zofia:
  Len:
  Ollie:
  Hale:
~~~~
wrist
-----
Kit: Wait. From the approach. I have the route, the door sequence, the cue. I have everything on this card.
Grace: Have you checked the pocket where you put the card you made so you wouldn't lose the other card?
Kit: Wrist. I've tied this one to my wrist.
Grace: Does your wrist know?
Kit: It has received written notice.
Zofia: The string. It's caught under your cuff.
Kit: Yes. That is deliberate. Mostly. Can you free it without untying it?
Grace: Hold still. There. Are we actually allowed to stand here, or is this another place somebody said would probably be fine?
Kit: Here. Our escort has cleared this spot. They made this placement just for me; it ends at the cue.
Zofia: Our last corridor permission. No chamber.
Kit: No chamber. Not even if someone you know goes through. Especially not then.
Grace: Good. Now show us what you're about to send.
Kit: Robing Room, Royal Gallery, Lords. The King goes that way. Black Rod comes towards the Commons to fetch the MPs.
Grace: But why do we still do this? Shut the door, then let the same person in?
Kit: Because the Commons can shut it against the Crown. I want to get the summons right. That doesn’t mean the door belongs to the King.
Grace: So they get to shut the door. Can they make him wait?
Kit: Wait. I want Dad to see me do this properly. But my cue can't make anybody answer your folder.
Grace: Then don't tell me the door does enough.
Kit: My cue comes before the slam. I need to check what comes before that.
Grace: Then put the cards down before you turn your whole wrist upside down.
Zofia: The paper under your thumb says NO SECOND CUE.
Kit: It still says that.
Zofia: You haven't left any space.
Kit: I know why you asked me to. I couldn't leave a space and let you think I had a way to use it.
Grace: Do you want me to hold the folder?
Zofia: Not yet.
Grace: That wasn't a request for it permanently.
Zofia: I need the undertaking page where I can reach it.
Kit: We can check the sequence now. Before anyone needs the cue. After that I have to watch for my signal.

cue
---
Zofia: The string. You could untie it.
Kit: I could untie it. The ceremony would still happen.
Zofia: Wait for the answer. Just until someone brings a reply.
Kit: No. I can give the right cue or fail to give it. I can't make more time by failing.
Zofia: A minute.
Kit: Zofia, I've checked the signal. I've checked the cards. If I say I need to check again, that would be another lie.
Zofia: You lied before.
Kit: Yes. That is why I'm telling you before I do it.
Grace: Has anyone actually said a reply's coming?
Zofia: Mara signed. So they have to answer now.
Grace: She promised to ask them. She didn't sign for them.
Zofia: I don't know how to stand here with only this page.
Grace: You can stand beside me.
Zofia: The horse is waiting for a load. I think that's what it is. It starts across my shoulders, before anything touches me.
Grace: Nothing has to touch you. Your bag is already too heavy.
Len: Reply, miss. Still on standby. [class=dead]
Len: This Historical Accounts Office. Never on our orders, miss. [class=dead]
Zofia: We made it up for the case. The unit account is still on hold. No answer.
Len: Policy. Yes, miss. Another spell of square-bashing. But the letter has somewhere to go when they've done with policy. [class=dead]
Zofia: Your reply address is in the file.
Len: File. Chit goes in; does an answer come out, miss? [class=dead]
Zofia: No. Not by itself.
Len: The duty you were asking for, miss. Orders to give reasons. [class=dead]
Zofia: The Records (Correction) Bill. It isn't law yet. Mara's still trying.
Len: Today. I wasn't asking them to finish everything today. Only to say what they sent us to do. [class=dead]
Zofia: I know. The promise to keep asking is real. It isn't the answer you asked for.
Kit: Signal. I'm giving the cue now.
Zofia: Kit—
Kit: Now.
Zofia: The door. It's shut.
Grace: I'm here.
Zofia: Len, it says “undertaking to pursue the purpose annot—” The bit about what they sent you to do. Hale, your reason, and an answer with reasons. She's signed for those. And the animals.
Zofia: First knock. She's promised to ask. That's all I've got.
Zofia: Second. There's a reviewer's name here for the animals. Still nothing about “voluntary”.
Zofia: Third. I'll keep asking. I don't know when—
Len: Then put the reply address beside the purpose, miss, so when they find the right page they can— [class=dead]
Hale: Madam, let my reason stand beside their charge; if the present arrangement denies me correction, let it state— [class=dead]


reply
-----
Zofia: Len?
Zofia: The reply address. The address you gave me for the letter home. I've kept it.
Ollie: What do you need me to write?
Zofia: The door opened before he finished.
Ollie: What did he actually say?
Zofia: Put the address beside the purpose. Then it stopped.
Ollie: Right. Those together. Give me the file when you can.
Zofia: It isn't a reply if we only send it to ourselves.
Ollie: No. But I can carry the address to the person who has to send one.

reasons
-------
Zofia: Hale?
Grace: Zofia. Look at me.
Zofia: The clause. He hadn't finished the clause.
Zofia: Hale, tell me what comes after “state”.
Grace: Tell me what you remember.
Zofia: I kept the original. You saw me cross that out. Hale?
Grace: Zofia. The door has opened. Come away from it with me.
Zofia: No. I'm listening to him. Don't make me answer you yet.
